IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er6-seat`

-- Worked cases for the seat layer (er6-seat). One or more per question, with the facts a real person in the seat would state.
-- Expected values are written from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt, lines 1709-2488), not copied from the rules' output.
-- Where the text leaves a day or a figure open (the day subsection 93(4.1) came into force, the day of royal assent of the Budget Implementation
-- Act, 2009, the day the Regulations SOR/2002-280 came into force) the case uses a TEST VALUE and says so; the answer is a function of that value.
-- The maximum weekly insurable earnings are the Act's (its Schedule II item 1, interim section 4(2), which names no year): $750.
-- Names in the comments (Amina, Ben ...) are made up.


§ `A1: Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 although I do not qualify under section 7 of the Act (reg 93(1))?`

-- Amina, caring for her new-born, has 650 hours and does not qualify under section 7: she qualifies under reg 93(1).
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650
-- 599 hours is one hour short of the 600 that reg 93(1)(b) asks for.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 599)
-- 600 hours is enough: "600 or more hours".
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 600
-- Ben already qualifies under section 7, so reg 93(1), which is for a person who does not, does not make him qualify.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE TRUE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650)
-- Chen claims regular benefits, which are not special benefits.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `a reason other than those mentioned in subsection 12(3)` TRUE 650)
-- Dana has had no interruption of earnings.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` FALSE 650)
-- Eli has never worked in insurable employment, so is not an insured person.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` FALSE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650)
-- Fatima claims sickness benefits with 800 hours.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `a prescribed illness, injury or quarantine` TRUE 800
-- Gus cares for a critically ill adult, 600 hours.
#ASSERT `Do I qualify for special benefits under regulation 93 with 600 or more hours` TRUE FALSE `care or support of a critically ill adult` TRUE 600

§ `A2: Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 when I make my initial claim (reg 93(2))?`

-- Amina makes her initial claim: a benefit period is established notwithstanding section 9.
#ASSERT `Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 on my initial claim` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 TRUE
-- She has not yet made an initial claim.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 on my initial claim` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 FALSE)
-- With 500 hours she does not qualify under reg 93(1), so no benefit period is established under it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Will a benefit period be established for me under regulation 93 on my initial claim` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 500 TRUE)

§ `A3: Are special benefits payable to me under regulation 93 for this week of my benefit period (reg 93(2))?`

-- A week of unemployment in the middle of her benefit period.
#ASSERT `Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2026 3 1)
-- The week begins Sunday 28 December 2025, before the benefit period begins on 4 January 2026.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2025 12 28))
-- The last week of the benefit period, 27 December 2026 to 2 January 2027, falls in it.
#ASSERT `Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 TRUE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2026 12 27)
-- The week is not a week of unemployment for her.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 TRUE FALSE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2026 3 1))
-- No initial claim, so no benefit period was established under reg 93(2).
#ASSERT NOT (`Are special benefits payable to me for this week of my benefit period under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 FALSE TRUE (YMD 2026 1 4) (YMD 2027 1 2) (YMD 2026 3 1))

§ `A4: Does a section among 22 to 23.3 of the Act apply to my special benefits under regulation 93 (reg 93(3))?`

-- Section 23 (new-born and adopted children) applies to Amina's special benefits under reg 93.
#ASSERT `Does the section of the Act apply to the payment of my special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 23
-- Section 23.3 (critically ill adults) is in the range.
#ASSERT `Does the section of the Act apply to the payment of my special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 23.3
-- Section 21 is outside "sections 22 to 23.3".
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the section of the Act apply to the payment of my special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 650 21)
-- If she does not qualify under reg 93(1) the sections do not apply to her under it.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the section of the Act apply to the payment of my special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE `caring for a new-born or adopted child` TRUE 400 23)

§ `A5: Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for a working day under regulation 93 (reg 93(4))?`

-- Emeka was ill on the day and would otherwise have been available, and can prove both.
#ASSERT `Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- Emeka can prove his illness but not his availability, and (4.1) does not help him.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Same, but he is paid under section 23 and claims for illness for a week that begins on or after the day (4.1) came into force: no need to prove availability.
#ASSERT `Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Same facts, but the week began before that day: (4.1) does not apply.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- He proves he was entitled to benefits under section 22 to 23.3 on the day, and nothing else.
#ASSERT `Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
-- He proves nothing.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
-- Availability alone, even with (4.1), is not enough.
#ASSERT NOT (`Have I proved enough to avoid being refused special benefits for the working day` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)

§ `A6: Am I excused from proving that I would have been available for work when I claim because of illness, injury or quarantine (reg 93(4.1))?`

-- Paid under section 23, claim for illness, week begins after the subsection came into force: excused.
#ASSERT `Am I excused from proving that I would otherwise have been available for work` TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- Not paid under sections 23 to 23.3: not excused.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from proving that I would otherwise have been available for work` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
-- The claim is not for illness, injury or quarantine: not excused.
#ASSERT NOT (`Am I excused from proving that I would otherwise have been available for work` TRUE FALSE TRUE)

§ `A7: After special benefits under regulation 93, can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for this week (reg 93(5))?`

-- Hana has received special benefits under reg 93; 100 + 600 = 700 equals the 700 the table asks for.
#ASSERT `Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE 100 600 700 TRUE TRUE
-- 99 + 600 = 699 is short of 700.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE 99 600 700 TRUE TRUE)
-- Section 18 bars payment for the week.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE 100 600 700 TRUE FALSE)
-- She has not received special benefits under reg 93.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` FALSE 100 600 700 TRUE TRUE)
-- Nothing is payable under the Act in the benefit period on her qualifying-period hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`Can I be paid regular benefits or additional special benefits for the week after special benefits under regulation 93` TRUE 100 600 700 FALSE TRUE)

§ `A8: Do the other provisions of the Act and of the Regulations apply to me while I claim under regulation 93 (reg 93(6))?`

-- Ibrahim claims under reg 93 and the regulation does not displace the provision.
#ASSERT `Does the provision of the Act or of the Regulations apply to me while I claim under regulation 93` TRUE FALSE
-- Reg 93 provides otherwise for the provision.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does the provision of the Act or of the Regulations apply to me while I claim under regulation 93` TRUE TRUE)

§ `B1: Which employment insurance region do I live in (Schedule I of the Regulations)?`

-- Joan lives in Ontario, Census Division No. 11, outside the Kingston agglomeration: Central Ontario (s 2(1.2)(a)).
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Ontario` 11 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Central Ontario`
-- Karim lives in the Quebec part of the Ottawa-Hull metropolitan area: Hull (s 3(10)).
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Quebec` 0 0 `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Hull`
-- Lena lives in the Ontario part: Ottawa (s 2(1)).
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Ontario` 0 0 `er6 Ottawa — Hull CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Ottawa`
-- Mo lives in St. John's metropolitan area, in census subdivision 01557 of division 1: Newfoundland/Labrador (s 11(2)(a)), not St. John's.
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Newfoundland` 1 1557 `er6 St. John’s CMA` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Newfoundland/Labrador`
-- Nia lives in Iqaluit (census subdivision 6204003): Iqaluit.
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Nunavut` 6204 6204003 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Iqaluit`
-- Census Division No. 99 of Ontario is in no region of the Schedule: the text does not answer.
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Ontario` 99 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Census Division No. 34 of Ontario, east of London, outside its metropolitan area: Niagara (s 2(9)(b)).
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` TRUE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Niagara`
-- Census Division No. 34 of Ontario, not east of London: Huron (s 2(12)(a)).
#ASSERT `Which employment insurance region do I live in` `er6 Ontario` 34 0 `er6 no Census Metropolitan Area` `er6 no Census Agglomeration` FALSE EQUALS JUST `er6 the region of Huron`

§ `B2: Is my region included in Pilot Project No. 6 (Schedule II.1)?`

