§ `C1: On a given day, was "hours" read as "weeks" in a provision of the Regulations (reg 94)?`

-- Pat asks whether subsection 93(5) read "hours" as "weeks" on 1 October 1996: yes.
#ASSERT `Was hours read as weeks in the provision on the day` `er6 subsection 93(5)` (YMD 1996 10 1)
-- On 5 January 1997 it no longer did.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was hours read as weeks in the provision on the day` `er6 subsection 93(5)` (YMD 1997 1 5))

§ `C2: How many hours does a week of insurable employment before 1997 stand for in my claim (reg 94.1)?`

-- Quinn's benefit period was established on 5 January 1997 and he presents evidence of a week worked in 1996: it stands for 35 hours.
#ASSERT `How many hours does a week of insurable employment before 1997 stand for in my claim` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE EQUALS JUST 35
-- A benefit period established on 4 January 1997 is outside reg 94.1.
#ASSERT `How many hours does a week of insurable employment before 1997 stand for in my claim` (YMD 1997 1 4) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `C3: Does regulation 94.2 apply to my claim (reg 94.2)?`

-- Quinn's claim of 1 February 1997 with evidence of 1996 employment: reg 94.2 applies.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 94.2 apply to my claim` (YMD 1997 2 1) TRUE
-- Without evidence of employment before 1997 it does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 94.2 apply to my claim` (YMD 1997 2 1) FALSE)

§ `C4: From which day do my weeks of insurable employment before 1997 count backward (reg 94.2(a))?`

-- Rita's last pay period of 1996 ran 15 to 28 December and she worked until 20 December: the weeks count back from 28 December.
#ASSERT `From which day do my weeks of insurable employment before 1997 count backward` (YMD 1996 12 28) (YMD 1996 12 15) (YMD 1996 12 20) EQUALS YMD 1996 12 28
-- She stopped working on 10 December, before that pay period: the weeks count back from 10 December.
#ASSERT `From which day do my weeks of insurable employment before 1997 count backward` (YMD 1996 12 28) (YMD 1996 12 15) (YMD 1996 12 10) EQUALS YMD 1996 12 10

§ `C5: For how many weeks are my insurable earnings considered to be (reg 94.2(b))?`

-- Sam has 52 weeks of insurable employment before 1997: his earnings are counted for the last 20.
#ASSERT `For how many weeks are my insurable earnings considered to be` 52 EQUALS 20
-- With 15 weeks they are counted for 15.
#ASSERT `For how many weeks are my insurable earnings considered to be` 15 EQUALS 15

§ `C6: Does regulation 94.3 apply to my last pay period beginning in December 1996 (reg 94.3)?`

-- Tess was paid for her last December pay period on 3 January 1997: reg 94.3 applies.
#ASSERT `Does regulation 94.3 apply to my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1997 1 3)
-- Paid on 31 December 1996, it does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does regulation 94.3 apply to my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1996 12 31))

§ `C7: As at which day must my employer read the Regulations to assess whether my last pay period of 1996 was insurable (reg 94.3(a))?`

-- Her employer assesses the insurability of that pay period under the Regulations as they read on 1 January 1997.
#ASSERT `As at which day must my employer read the Regulations to assess my last pay period of 1996` (YMD 1997 1 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1997 1 1)
-- Paid in 1996: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `As at which day must my employer read the Regulations to assess my last pay period of 1996` (YMD 1996 12 30) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `C8: How many hours of insurable employment am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996 (reg 94.3(b))?`

-- Tess worked 40, 20 and 35 hours in the three weeks of that pay period that fall in 1996: 40 + 35 + 35 = 110 hours.
#ASSERT `How many hours am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1997 1 3) 3 40 20 35 0 0 EQUALS JUST 110
-- One week, 10 hours: she counts for 35.
#ASSERT `How many hours am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1997 1 3) 1 10 0 0 0 0 EQUALS JUST 35
-- Six weeks is more than the form takes: the text is not answered.
#ASSERT `How many hours am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1997 1 3) 6 0 0 0 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paid in 1996: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `How many hours am I determined to have worked in my last pay period beginning in December 1996` (YMD 1996 12 31) 3 40 20 35 0 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `C9: How many hours do my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier convert into (reg 94.4)?`

-- Section 59.1 applies on 6 January 1997 and needs 10 insured weeks of 1996 or earlier: 350 hours.
#ASSERT `How many hours do my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier convert into` (YMD 1997 1 6) TRUE 10 EQUALS JUST 350
-- "After January 5, 1997": on 5 January itself it does not.
#ASSERT `How many hours do my insured weeks in 1996 or earlier convert into` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE 10 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `C10: What is the hourly equivalent of the weeks that section 59.1(2) of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations requires of me (reg 94.4)?`

-- Paragraphs 59.1(2)(a) and (b) require 12 weeks: 420 hours.
#ASSERT `What is the hourly equivalent of the weeks that section 59.1 of the Unemployment Insurance Regulations requires of me` (YMD 1997 1 6) TRUE 12 EQUALS JUST 420

§ `C11: Was a provision of the Regulations in force on a given day (reg 95)?`

-- Sections 10 to 12 came into force on 1 January 1997.
#ASSERT `Was the provision of the Regulations in force on the day` `er6 sections 10 to 12` (YMD 1997 1 1)
-- They were not in force on 31 December 1996.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the provision of the Regulations in force on the day` `er6 sections 10 to 12` (YMD 1996 12 31))
-- Section 34 and the Table to 55(7) came into force on 5 January 1997, not 4 January.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was the provision of the Regulations in force on the day` `er6 sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c)` (YMD 1997 1 4))
-- Any other provision was in force from 30 June 1996.
#ASSERT `Was the provision of the Regulations in force on the day` `er6 any other provision of these Regulations` (YMD 1996 6 30)

§ `C12: Did the provision in Part I of Schedule III apply on a given day (reg 95(4))?`

-- Part I of Schedule III applied on 31 December 1996.
#ASSERT `Did the provision in Part I of Schedule III apply on the day` (YMD 1996 12 31)
-- Not on 1 January 1997.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the provision in Part I of Schedule III apply on the day` (YMD 1997 1 1))

§ `C13: Did the provision in Part I.1 of Schedule III apply in place of section 12 on a given day (reg 95(4.1))?`

-- Part I.1 applied from 12 September 1996.
#ASSERT `Did the provision in Part I.1 of Schedule III apply in place of section 12 on the day` (YMD 1996 9 12)
-- Not on 11 September 1996.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did the provision in Part I.1 of Schedule III apply in place of section 12 on the day` (YMD 1996 9 11))

§ `C14: Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on a given day (reg 95(5))?`

-- Part II applied in place of sections 19 to 21 on 31 December 1996.
#ASSERT `Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` (YMD 1996 12 31)
-- Not on 1 January 1997, when they came into force.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 19 to 21 on the day` (YMD 1997 1 1))

§ `C15: Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34, the Table to subsection 55(7) and paragraph 93(1)(c) on a given day (reg 95(5))?`

-- Part II applied in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34 and the Table on 4 January 1997.
#ASSERT `Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34 and the Table to subsection 55(7) on the day` (YMD 1997 1 4)
-- Not on 5 January 1997.
#ASSERT NOT (`Did Part II of Schedule III apply in place of sections 22 to 24 and 34 and the Table to subsection 55(7) on the day` (YMD 1997 1 5))

§ `D1: Does the old section 77.1 govern how low-earning weeks are excluded from my benefit rate (SOR/2001-495 s 4)?`

-- Una's benefit period was established on 17 November 2001: the old section 77.1 governs.
#ASSERT `Does section 77.1 as it read before 18 November 2001 govern the exclusion of my low-earning weeks` (YMD 2001 11 17)
-- One established on 18 November 2001 is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does section 77.1 as it read before 18 November 2001 govern the exclusion of my low-earning weeks` (YMD 2001 11 18))

§ `D2: Do the Regulations SOR/2002-280 apply to my benefit period (SOR/2002-280 s 2)?`

-- Vik's benefit period commences on 5 January 2003; the amending Regulations came into force on 17 November 2002 (a test value): they apply.
#ASSERT `Do the Regulations SOR/2002-280 apply to my benefit period` (YMD 2003 1 5) (YMD 2002 11 17)
-- A benefit period commencing the day before they came into force is not covered.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the Regulations SOR/2002-280 apply to my benefit period` (YMD 2002 11 16) (YMD 2002 11 17))

§ `D3: Does Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 decide the maximum weeks of benefits I can be paid (2009, c. 2, s. 225)?`

-- Wen is a claimant referred to in 55(7); her benefit period of 7 June 2009 to 5 June 2010 had not ended before 1 March 2009 (the second Sunday before royal assent on Thursday 12 March 2009, a test value) and began before 12 September 2010: Schedule 10 decides.
#ASSERT `Does Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 decide the maximum weeks of benefits I can be paid` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12)
-- A benefit period that began on 12 September 2010 is outside.
#ASSERT NOT (`Does Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 decide the maximum weeks of benefits I can be paid` TRUE (YMD 2010 9 12) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12))

§ `D4: What is the maximum number of weeks of benefits I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009 (2009, c. 2, s. 225)?`

-- With 700 hours Schedule 10 gives 19 weeks.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12) 700 EQUALS JUST 19
-- A benefit period that ended on 28 February 2009, before the second Sunday, is outside: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2009 2 28) (YMD 2009 3 12) 700 EQUALS NOTHING
-- 1820 hours or more gives 41 weeks.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid under Schedule 10 to the Budget Implementation Act, 2009` TRUE (YMD 2009 6 7) (YMD 2010 6 5) (YMD 2009 3 12) 2000 EQUALS JUST 41

§ `D5: On which day did section 77.6 (Pilot Project No. 10) cease to have effect (2009, c. 2, s. 226(1))?`

-- With royal assent on Thursday 12 March 2009 (test value), section 77.6 ceased to have effect on Saturday 28 February 2009, the second Saturday before.
#ASSERT `On which day did section 77.6 cease to have effect` (YMD 2009 3 12) EQUALS YMD 2009 2 28

§ `D6: What is the maximum number of weeks of benefits I can be paid as a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10 (2009, c. 2, s. 226(2))?`

-- Xia is in Pilot Project No. 10 and her benefit period ended on 1 March 2009 or later: the Act's Schedule I figure, 38 weeks here (a test figure).
#ASSERT `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid as a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10` TRUE (YMD 2009 3 1) (YMD 2009 3 12) 38 EQUALS JUST 38
-- Her benefit period ended on 28 February 2009: not covered.
#ASSERT `What is the maximum number of weeks I can be paid as a claimant in Pilot Project No. 10` TRUE (YMD 2009 2 28) (YMD 2009 3 12) 38 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `D7: How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 3)?`

-- Yara's benefit period was established on 7 June 2009; she contributed at least 30% in 7 of the last 10 years: 25 weeks become 30.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 0 0 0 0 0 25 EQUALS JUST 30
-- In 12 of the last 15 years: 20 more weeks, 45.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2009 6 7) 0 0 0 0 0 12 25 EQUALS JUST 45
-- She was paid 36 weeks of regular benefits in the 260 weeks before: the section does not apply.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 36 (YMD 2009 6 7) 7 0 0 0 0 0 25 EQUALS NOTHING
-- No contribution record that qualifies: the section applies but adds nothing.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 3 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2009 6 7) 0 0 0 0 0 0 25 EQUALS JUST 25

§ `D8: How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 4 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 4)?`

-- A benefit period established on 20 June 2010 with 12 of the last 15 years: 30 weeks plus 15 is 45.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 4 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2010 6 20) 0 0 0 0 0 12 30 EQUALS JUST 45

§ `D9: How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 5 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 5)?`

-- One established on 20 July 2010 with 10 of the last 13 years: 30 + 4 = 34.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 5 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2010 7 20) 0 0 0 10 0 0 30 EQUALS JUST 34

§ `D10: How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 6 of the Act 2009, c. 30 (2009, c. 30, s. 6)?`

-- One established on 20 August 2010 with 13 of the last 15 years: 41 + 5 = 46.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 6 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2010 8 20) 0 0 0 0 0 13 41 EQUALS JUST 46
-- One established on 12 September 2010 is outside section 6.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits am I deemed to have under section 6 of the Act 2009 c 30` TRUE 20 (YMD 2010 9 12) 0 0 0 0 0 13 41 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `D11: What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine (2009, c. 30, s. 7)?`

-- Zed is outside Canada and sections 3 to 6 apply; the section 225 maximum is 55: the combined weeks cannot exceed 55.
#ASSERT `What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE 55 EQUALS JUST 55
-- If the maximum is 45 the cap is 50.
#ASSERT `What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine` TRUE FALSE TRUE 45 EQUALS JUST 50
-- If the benefit period has been extended under 10(13) to (13.3), the deemed text does not apply.
#ASSERT `What is the greatest total number of weeks of benefits I can combine` TRUE TRUE TRUE 55 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `D12: Which version of subsection 55(4) of the Regulations governs my claim (SOR/2012-260 s 4)?`

-- Abe is a claimant referred to in 55(4) with a benefit period established on 8 December 2012: the old subsection 55(4) continues to apply.
#ASSERT `Which version of subsection 55(4) governs my claim` TRUE (YMD 2012 12 8) EQUALS JUST `er6 the version that read immediately before December 9, 2012`
-- Established on 9 December 2012: the new one.
#ASSERT `Which version of subsection 55(4) governs my claim` TRUE (YMD 2012 12 9) EQUALS JUST `er6 the version enacted by the amending regulations`
-- Not a claimant referred to in 55(4): the provision does not speak.
#ASSERT `Which version of subsection 55(4) governs my claim` FALSE (YMD 2012 12 8) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `D13: Which version of subsection 55.01(3) of the Regulations governs my claim (SOR/2012-260 s 5)?`

-- Bea is a self-employed person referred to in 55.01(3), benefit period established 8 December 2012: the old subsection.
#ASSERT `Which version of subsection 55.01(3) governs my claim` TRUE (YMD 2012 12 8) EQUALS JUST `er6 the version that read immediately before December 9, 2012`
-- Established on 9 December 2012: the new one.
#ASSERT `Which version of subsection 55.01(3) governs my claim` TRUE (YMD 2012 12 9) EQUALS JUST `er6 the version enacted by the amending regulations`

§ `D14: Do the former rules for allocating earnings (before 25 September 2022) still apply to my earnings (2022, c. 10, s. 350.1)?`

-- Cal applied for benefits; his earnings would be allocated to weeks the first of which begins on 2 January 2022: the former rules continue to apply.
#ASSERT `Do the former rules for allocating earnings still apply to my earnings` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2022 1 2)
-- If the first week begins on 25 September 2022 they do not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the former rules for allocating earnings still apply to my earnings` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2022 9 25))
-- If the first week began on 26 September 2021 they do (the first day of the window).
#ASSERT `Do the former rules for allocating earnings still apply to my earnings` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2021 9 26)

§ `E1: Was my employment in this week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little (Schedule III, Part I, s 6.1)?`

-- Dee earned 140 and worked 10 hours in a week of July 1996 when the maximum was 750 (the Act's interim figure): 20 per cent is 150, so under it and under 15 hours: her employment was excluded.
#ASSERT `Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` (YMD 1996 7 14) 140 10 750 FALSE `er6 seat a multiple of a week` 2 0 0 FALSE FALSE
-- She earned 150: not under 20 per cent of 750.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` (YMD 1996 7 14) 150 10 750 FALSE `er6 seat a multiple of a week` 2 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
-- She worked 15 hours.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` (YMD 1996 7 14) 140 15 750 FALSE `er6 seat a multiple of a week` 2 0 0 FALSE FALSE)
-- Her pay was for a fortnight (two weeks) and the 300 earned in it, with earnings in each week, meets the exception (2 x 150): not excluded.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` (YMD 1996 7 14) 140 10 750 TRUE `er6 seat a multiple of a week` 2 300 0 TRUE FALSE)
-- The same week in February 1997 is outside Part I.
#ASSERT NOT (`Was my employment in the week excluded from insurable employment because I earned and worked so little` (YMD 1997 2 1) 140 10 750 FALSE `er6 seat a multiple of a week` 2 0 0 FALSE FALSE)

§ `E2: Do my cash earnings or hours for my longer pay period reach what is required, so that section 6.1(1) does not exclude my employment (Schedule III, Part I, s 6.1(2))?`

-- A semi-monthly pay period with cash earnings of 325 in each week: 2 1/6 times 150, the exception applies.
#ASSERT `Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period` 2 325 0 TRUE FALSE 750
-- 324 is short of 325.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` `er6 seat a semi-monthly pay period` 2 324 0 TRUE FALSE 750)
-- A monthly pay period with 65 hours worked in each week: the exception applies.
#ASSERT `Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` `er6 seat a monthly pay period` 2 0 65 FALSE TRUE 750
-- Seven days beginning on a Monday with 15 hours: the exception applies without the "each".
#ASSERT `Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 2 0 15 FALSE FALSE 750
-- Three periods of seven days with 450 (3 x 150) and earnings in each: the exception applies.
#ASSERT `Do my cash earnings or hours for my pay period reach what section 6.1(2) requires` `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 3 450 0 TRUE FALSE 750

§ `E3: Is this week a prescribed week (Schedule III, Part I.1, s 12)?`

-- Eve served a week of the waiting period in October 1996: a prescribed week.
#ASSERT `Is the week a prescribed week` (YMD 1996 10 6) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
-- Her week of a labour dispute counts too.
#ASSERT `Is the week a prescribed week` (YMD 1996 10 6) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- A week with none of the ten kinds is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the week a prescribed week` (YMD 1996 10 6) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
-- The same facts in January 1997 are outside Part I.1.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the week a prescribed week` (YMD 1997 1 12) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

§ `E4: Must my employer complete a record of employment for me (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(1))?`

-- Fay's employer employs her in insurable employment and her earnings were interrupted on 1 August 1996: it must complete her record of employment.
#ASSERT `Must my employer complete a record of employment for me` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE TRUE
-- Without an interruption of earnings there is no duty.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer complete a record of employment for me` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE)
-- An interruption beginning on 1 January 1997 is outside Part II item 2.
#ASSERT NOT (`Must my employer complete a record of employment for me` (YMD 1997 1 1) TRUE TRUE)

§ `E5: By what day must my employer deliver or mail my copies of the record of employment (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(2))?`

-- Her interruption began on 1 August 1996 and her employer became aware on 3 August: five days after the later, 8 August.
#ASSERT `By what day must my employer deliver or mail my copies of the record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 1) (YMD 1996 8 3) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1996 8 8)
-- If the employer was aware on 1 August and the interruption began on 5 August: 10 August.
#ASSERT `By what day must my employer deliver or mail my copies of the record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 5) (YMD 1996 8 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1996 8 10)

§ `E6: Until what day must my employer keep my copies of the record of employment if it could not deliver them (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(3))?`

-- The employer could not deliver by 8 August 1996 and nobody asked: it keeps the copies until 7 August 1997, 52 weeks after.
#ASSERT `Until what day must my employer keep my copies of the record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 8) FALSE (YMD 1996 8 8) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1997 8 7)
-- Fay asked for them on 1 September 1996: until then.
#ASSERT `Until what day must my employer keep my copies of the record of employment` (YMD 1996 8 8) TRUE (YMD 1996 9 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 1996 9 1)

§ `E7: Are sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations kept out of the way the weeks and earnings in my record of employment are worked out (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(4))?`

-- Sections 35 and 36 are kept out of the way her record of employment is worked out (interruption on 1 August 1996).
#ASSERT `Are sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations kept out of the way my record of employment is worked out` (YMD 1996 8 1)
-- Not for an interruption in 1997.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are sections 35 and 36 of the Regulations kept out of the way my record of employment is worked out` (YMD 1997 1 1))

§ `E8: May my employer estimate my earnings for my last pay period (Schedule III, Part II, s 19(5))?`

-- Her pay period was current when she was laid off and her earnings cannot be ascertained with accuracy: the employer may estimate.
#ASSERT `May my employer estimate my earnings for my last pay period` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE TRUE
-- If her earnings can be ascertained it may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May my employer estimate my earnings for my last pay period` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE)

§ `E9: May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings instead of a record of employment (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(1))?`

-- Her employer failed to deliver a record of employment: she may give a statement.
#ASSERT `May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE
-- Its records are lost: likewise.
#ASSERT `May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE TRUE
-- Neither: no.
#ASSERT NOT (`May I give a statement of my employment history and insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE FALSE)

§ `E10: On which day does the first of my weeks of insurable employment begin (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(2))?`

-- Four weeks of insurable employment ending with the week beginning Sunday 15 December 1996 begin on 24 November 1996.
#ASSERT `On which day does the first of my weeks of insurable employment begin` (YMD 1996 12 2) (YMD 1996 12 15) 4 EQUALS JUST (YMD 1996 11 24)

§ `E11: How many weeks of insurable employment count in my employment period (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(3))?`

-- Her record reports 30 weeks but only 25 weeks or part weeks fall in her employment period: 25.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of insurable employment count in my employment period` (YMD 1996 8 1) 30 25 EQUALS JUST 25
-- Reported 20 of 25: 20.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of insurable employment count in my employment period` (YMD 1996 8 1) 20 25 EQUALS JUST 20

§ `E12: May the Commission work out my insurable weeks and earnings from the records my bankrupt employer's trustee gave it (Schedule III, Part II, s 20(4))?`

-- Her employer is bankrupt, nobody gave the Commission her record of employment, and the trustee gave it the payroll records: the Commission may use them.
#ASSERT `May the Commission work out my insurable weeks and earnings from my bankrupt employer's trustee's records` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- If the trustee gave no records it may not.
#ASSERT NOT (`May the Commission work out my insurable weeks and earnings from my bankrupt employer's trustee's records` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE)

§ `E13: Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings (Schedule III, Part II, s 22)?`

-- A premium was payable on her earnings: they are taken into account (1 August 1996).
#ASSERT `Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE
-- No premium was payable: they are not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE)
-- On 5 January 1997 the interim section 22 no longer applies.
#ASSERT NOT (`Are my earnings taken into account in working out my average weekly insurable earnings` (YMD 1997 1 5) TRUE)

§ `E14: How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period (Schedule III, Part II, s 23)?`

-- Gil was paid for seven days beginning on a Wednesday: 3 pay periods, each with 150 (20 per cent of the maximum 750) earned in each: 3 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period` (YMD 1996 8 1) `er6 seat seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 2 150 0 TRUE FALSE 3 750 EQUALS JUST 3
-- Hal was paid for two periods of seven days and earned 300 in them with earnings in each: 2 weeks.
#ASSERT `How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period` (YMD 1996 8 1) `er6 seat more than one period of seven consecutive days beginning on a day other than Sunday` 2 300 0 TRUE FALSE 1 750 EQUALS JUST 2
-- A monthly pay period is not in section 23.
#ASSERT `How many weeks are taken as weeks of insurable employment for my pay period` (YMD 1996 8 1) `er6 seat a monthly pay period` 2 5000 0 TRUE FALSE 1 750 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `E15: Is this person my dependant, or my spouse's dependant (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(1))?`

-- His niece is related to him in the manner of subsection 251(6) of the Income Tax Act: a dependant (August 1996).
#ASSERT `Is the person my dependant or my spouse's dependant` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE
-- A stranger is not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Is the person my dependant or my spouse's dependant` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE)

§ `E16: Is this person my spouse (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(2))?`

-- The person married to the claimant is the spouse.
#ASSERT `Is the person my spouse` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE
-- A person described in 252(4) of the Income Tax Act is too.
#ASSERT `Is the person my spouse` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE TRUE

§ `E17: Do the circumstances that the Regulations prescribe for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me (Schedule III, Part II, s 34(3))?`

-- A child tax benefit is payable to his spouse in the month of the claim: the prescribed circumstances exist.
#ASSERT `Do the circumstances prescribed for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me` (YMD 1996 8 1) TRUE FALSE
-- He supports a dependant: they exist.
#ASSERT `Do the circumstances prescribed for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE TRUE
-- Neither: they do not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do the circumstances prescribed for the benefit rate of paragraph 14(1)(b) exist for me` (YMD 1996 8 1) FALSE FALSE)

§ `E18: How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me for my weeks of insurable employment (Schedule III, Part II, item 5)?`

-- Ida has 30 weeks of insurable employment (a claim of 1 August 1996): the interim Table gives 19 weeks of benefits.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me` (YMD 1996 8 1) 30 EQUALS JUST 19
-- With 11 weeks the Table, which starts at 12, does not answer.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me` (YMD 1996 8 1) 11 EQUALS NOTHING
-- On 5 January 1997 the interim Table has been replaced.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of benefits does the interim Table to subsection 55(7) give me` (YMD 1997 1 5) 30 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `E19: Do I have the 20 weeks of insurable employment that the interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for (Schedule III, Part II, item 6)?`

-- Jo has 20 weeks of insurable employment in her qualifying period (August 1996): she has what interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for.
#ASSERT `Do I have the 20 weeks of insurable employment that the interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for` (YMD 1996 8 1) 20
-- With 19 she does not.
#ASSERT NOT (`Do I have the 20 weeks of insurable employment that the interim paragraph 93(1)(c) asks for` (YMD 1996 8 1) 19)
